{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvackyK7c18j7gHNTGDA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Recommendation: don't remove it yet. Keep it at 10%, fix the measurement, and decide against criteria set in advance.**\n\n**Why the 4% isn't a verdict**\n- **Missing data:** Five of 14 days are missing, so 4% is probably an undercount. Anyone who first tried the feature on an outage day may be missing entirely. We can't tell whether the true figure is 4% or 7%.\n- **No benchmark:** Nobody has said what adoption should be. 4% trial in two weeks could be fine for a feature that only matters to people with busy calendars.\n- **Trial isn't the right measure:** The more useful questions are whether people who try it use it again, and whether the events it creates get kept or deleted.\n- **Discoverability:** Low adoption could mean the feature is hard to find rather than unwanted. Removal would treat both causes the same.\n\n**Bounded next step (about a week)**\n1. **Backfill the gap:** Use data that doesn't depend on the broken pipeline, such as server logs or the database records of auto-scheduled events. Check whether those numbers diverge from the pipeline's.\n2. **Build a funnel:** Track exposed, saw it, tried it, used it again. This shows whether the problem is discovery, trust, or value.\n3. **Check absolute counts:** 10% of users may be a small sample, so confirm how many people the 4% represents.\n4. **Set criteria now:** For example, \"if repeat use among triers is below X% after another two clean weeks, we cut or rework it.\"\n5. **Add pipeline monitoring:** An alert on event volume would have caught the outage within a day.\n\nKeeping the feature at 10% costs little and is easy to undo. Removing it on partial data would be hard to reverse once users have built habits around it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3825,"cache_read_input_tokens":4609,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3825},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e878cf4f-c51c-4b96-b2b7-9845db3b8508","uuid":"3b5e2846-2085-425c-8520-4887239c1b03","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:07:55.154Z","request_id":"req_011Cfvackigftkejjk78W3md"}
